Notebook of a [fictitious] poli-sci professor, Mr. O, who believes he was encamped with Che Guevara during his 1967 attempted revolution in Bolivia, and later ensconced in a spy mission in Cuba.The book focusses on the romanticization of the revolutionary, and political violence, preceded of course, by the romanticization of colonial conquest which inevitably led to those same revolutions. Drawing from real and imagined sources - including Che's diary and actual and concocted photographs - Deschamp's interweaving of fantasy and history suggests their strong idelogical relationship.--From publisher website.
